Z||000015||007DOUG||12-31-2000||01:42 AM||||DON'T BELIEVE EVERYTHING THE MEDIA REPORTS!!!<P>I was really hoping everyone would "blow off" the media after the Y2K scare at this very time last year. I seem to recall a day when there were investigative reporters. Now everything is "according to our source", or based totally on hear-say<P>When a company reports its "lowest sales ever", doesn't mean they are bankrupt. It just means they made $3 billion this year instead of the $5 billion they made last year.<P>I live in one of the "armpits" of America. You can find plenty of minimum wage jobs here, but CAREER jobs are hard to find. However, you won't have any trouble finding everyone at the mall/restaurants on the weekends. The economy is steady.<P>I will make one prediction based on my own observation.........We can't continue to pay $7-$10 an hour and still expect folks to afford their mortgage (or rent), pay the utilites, buy $20K cars, prepare for retirement, and well..... JUST PLAIN LIVE!!!!   <P>A BIG economic crash IS coming, But I don't think its soon.<P>Sorry, I'm done ranting. Doug<P>P.S. cut-up your credit cards||||reg||6
Z||000016||Tweek||12-31-2000||03:29 AM||||A note abour losing our jobs... =) I got hired at the company I work at 1 year ago. We had 850 employees. We now have very close to 2000. I work on a contract for a dot.com, namely MSN.com (And YES they suck bad.. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )If they go out of business, we'ed be in trouble. heheh I went and cleaned my 2m4 off 4 times during my shift at work today, and it wasn't evn snowing when I got there, it was snowing sideways!! Well, im rambling. Cheers!<P>-Ted||||reg||10
Z||000017||kslish||12-31-2000||05:31 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rockcrawl:<BR><B>There was one good point on that list:<P>Apple computer is almost out of business!<P>It's about time!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Glad you told me, since Apple is my second employer (I work for them part time).  Guess I better look for another job!!<P>I'm just sick of Apple being the whipping boy of the press.  If I had a dollar for every "Apple is going out of business" story, I'd be a millionaire.  They've only been re-running the same story for the past 20 years.  It would be pretty hard for a company with 1.4 billion (yes, BILLION) dollars stockpiled away to be in that bad of shape. They are certainly better off right now than they were during the last "recession" of the mid-90's.<P>They're stock price does suck though, but then again so does every tech stock right now. That and computer sales are pretty low for the entire industry right now for both Macs and Wintel machines (Gateway and Compaq are being hit hard by the press also, even Microsoft hasn't been immune due to Windows ME being a rather huge flop in upgrade sales). Until someone comes out with a killer new app (not just a new version of Windows or Office) that requires newer and faster computers, people aren't going to replace their current computers that do pretty much everything they want to right now anyways.  Simple economics.  I don't need a 1.5 Ghz machine to download my MP3's with Napster.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Also, the best reason for Apple staying in business into the far, far future?  Microsoft would never let Apple die, otherwise they truely would be a monopoly.<P>Don't believe everything you read in the papers.  The mostly-biased press is part of the reason the economy is faltering anyways.<P>Too keep this Fiero related, I'd probably resort to living in my Fiero before selling it anyways.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Ken S.<BR>Still enjoying getting my paycheck in the mail from Apple<BR>'87 GT and '86 SC<BR>Pittsburgh, PA<BR>||||reg||13
Z||000018||Wolfhound||12-31-2000||06:28 AM||||Cheevers2, Yep, Dripping with Sarcasm  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000019||Tryxalon||12-31-2000||09:56 AM||||Bad economy? Recession? With a 2.9% GNP rate of Growth?  <P>ROFLMAO!! <P>You are just "lost in space" because because you are used to the results of those "Voodoo Reaganomics"  a 3-4% GPN Rate of growth for the last 13 years!! DESPITE the worst that the Clinton Administration can do!<P>Oh ye of little faith!!! <BR>If Greenspan cuts prime interest rates .25 and or Shrubya gives a tax cut our growth rate will jump to 4% per year or likely 6 or more.<P>Besides, if we were to go into a recession, the posession of a Fiero is a benefit!! <P>Doesn't use as much gas as a Huge Honkin' SUV (and we all know that there is only one person in each of those damn things!). <P>With so few enlightened individuals, our cars cannot depreciate any more (and good, scarce items will always appreciate just got to let them get more scarce).<P> It is cheaper to continue to maintain an older car than to buy a new one. <P>And if one Fiero Parts supplier goes out of business, another will arise - AS LONG AS THERE IS DEMAND!! <P>Seems to me that the fun, thrifty, economical, safe, (add your adjective here) Fiero is the BEST car to have - recession or not. <P>So what cha worried 'bout?? <P>   <P><p>[This message has been edited by Tryxalon (edited 12-31-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000020||MrPBody||12-31-2000||10:10 AM||||There's nothing like a good scare to sell newspapers.  Like Y2K, it's probably not as bad as it sounds.<P>On the other hand, I think there is some reason for Dubya-phobia.  Before the '92 election, someone asked "Why are we blaming George Bush for this recession?  It's all part of the normal business cycle."  So . . . what drives the business cycle?  Greed.  Plain blind human greed.  I don't expect Dubya's administration to discourage greed, so I'm looking for wilder economic swings like those under Reagan and Bush, Sr.<P>Sell our Fieros?  Bad idea.  We might have to live in them.<BR>||||reg||1
