Z||000022||BAM-BAM||12-31-2000||12:07 PM||||  The trouble with our economy people is "US". We are what is wrong with the state of things today. It seems that every one wants more for less, and no one is willing to do their share. That philosophy has tricked into every walk of our society.  <BR>  It starts with the government and big buisness and works it's way eventually to you and me. Like all things in nature, we too take the path of least resistance and or, go with the flow. Now I'm not talking about anyone here in particular or even for that matter, any one who represents this forum, rather we as a people, as a whole.<BR>  I am a union worker and I feel that unions are both neccessary and evil. First off, if it weren't for unions, there would be no economy today, we would all be bigger slaves to industry. Secondly, you can pretty much blame the economy on the unions. It's a parodox. We have unions to insure fair labor and decent wages. However, have you seen or been through a union negotiation? It's all about "WE WANT MORE, WE WANT MORE" More money,higher wages, better bennifits, more vacation, more sick time; and what do we give in return? Less productivity. We also want longer breaks, increased lunch time, flex time, comptime. It's rediculous. I only speak what I have experienced and I don't intend on offending anyone.<BR>  Look at the cost of automobiles. I heard somewhere and it may be wrong, that it dosen't cost much more to manufacture an auto mobile now than it did twenty five years ago, yet the price of autos has risen astronomicaly. What have the auto manufacturers done? they have used less expensive products in the manufacuring of vehicals, they have moved their plants out of the country and employed workers at far lower wages, they have laid off 10's of thousands of American and Canadian workers and raised the price of their vehicals. It's all about profitt. Did you know that the earnings loss statements that are published are after all debts and incumbrences? That's right, after every one has been paid that's how much they made or lost. The truth is they(the big corps) have never lost. They just didn't make as much one year or made more one year. If you work all year at a set wage with no overtime or bonus then the next year you worked 1000 hrs. overtime and got a $500.00 safety bonus, what do you do with that money? We spend it and so do the big companies. Then the next year you aren't graced with the inflated income and you begin to falter and you feel like you lost because you cant make the payment on that new Dodge Durango. You feel in efect that you have lost money. You see these big business people aren't as smart as we give them credit. Oh they take care of themselves, but they drive their companies into the ground, all the while killing people like you and me. You want to stop the price of vehicals from rising so high? Quit buying them! Don't pay the prices, it's rediculous. If everyone boycotted the big car manufaturers for two months, they would lower their prices. <P> Whats the answer to all of this? It's simple. Look around you, look at your neigbor or the guy or gal walking down the street. Ask yourself how, what you may do today at work will effect that person or those peole. Ask yourself if you are giving an honest effort for your wage. Ask yourself how, what that person does at work today will effect you. We as a people are all self absorbed. we care nothing about the people around us and how our actions effect the world around us. But we expect the world around us to take us into consideration. That philosophy starts at the top and works it's way down to you and me. Then again it all starts with you and me. It's a paradox,  "WE WANT MORE FOR LESS" and "WE GET LESS FOR MORE". <P>   Think about it.<P> Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach/KYB Susp.<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats,headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Gauges And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||1
Z||000023||ur2biteme||01-01-2001||12:05 AM||||jesus bam, how much thought did that take!??!!?  that was a mouthful, BUT TRUE!<P>------------------<BR>UR2BITEME<BR>'87 econo coupe<BR>170k and a bad fender :(||||reg||1
